Content:
@Tyler Craig thank you!
What you just said does create a light bulb moment for me. It seems that maybe this team just needed a leader. All of those other factors (lack of cohesion, training, preparedness in their roles), could possibly simply stem from not having a true leader (and in the leader/facilitator role) to keep the wheels from falling off.
I've been trying to think from the perspective of my role as the Delivery Specialist for this specific prompt, but I haven't found much. I would say that when it comes to delivery, all of the members certainly needed to consider and adjust their tones and overall approach to each other. Their communication styles were nary on the professional spectrum.
